17592186051867 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051867 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ed99a2e9-9e65-5722-b045-05d6294b9253" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054365 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054365 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following statement:\n\n$14$ is divisible by $4$ **or** $\\sqrt{3}$ is a rational number.\n\nWrite this statement in symbolic form using the following notations:\n\n- ![](images/64/64c5006a1d5f6b515ebfb603e5da3d10b44616960afd0dbbcabb32a5a23aed26.svg)\n\n- ![](images/b2/b2d623c77373a42771d812e0242d4545884a79107c1e97769d0f4bb8bb7a7a06.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054365 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8c9f90f-3c97-5a01-99b5-9a9f8b3eef66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054365 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{14 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is divisible by }\\vphantom{p} 4 }_S \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\sqrt{3} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a rational number} }_T,\n$$\n\nthat is, $S \\lor T.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054366 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12678" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054366 #edb/ref 1071 "$7$ is odd **or** a multiple of $3$, **and** $3$ is less than $7$.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- ![](images/c9/c99c7535c3d2d6c854aea2e3408d15f2c0ff6423c4010ad211dbb6d576fe6928.svg)\n\n- ![](images/3f/3fca3aace2f71ead6ca860e93e9138abb40559e0eb9434ca068b563380b12912.svg)\n\n- ![](images/76/768f38af5ffc9fc48817db2f054dc9da251a26469a644c0e7eb7141fef54284b.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054366 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5a60113-14a0-5468-93b1-7f0eaa6e9a90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054366 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is odd or a multiple of $3.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd }}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a multiple of }3}_Q,\n$$\n\nthat is, $P \\lor Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3$ is less than $7$. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is odd} \\textbf{ or } \\vphantom{p} \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ a multiple of } 3}_{P \\, \\lor \\,Q}, \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \n\\underbrace{3 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is less than } 7 }_R\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P \\lor Q) \\land R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054368 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12693" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054368 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{5 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is prime} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textbf{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{\\dfrac13 \\in \\mathbb{Z}}_B\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $A$ and $B,$ and the compound statement $A\\lor B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054368 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6497cb54-2453-5dd7-8b97-09e06280d774" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054368 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\frac{1}{3}\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054389 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12895" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054389 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following compound statement:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\mathbb{Z}\\cup \\mathbb{R}=\\mathbb{Z} }_P \n\\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 21}^Q \n\\quad \\overbrace{\\vphantom{|}\\textbf{or}}^{\\lor} \\quad \n\\overbrace{7 \\,|\\, 29}^R }_{Q \\, \\lor \\, R}\n$$\n\nFind the truth values of the statements $P,$ $Q$ and $R,$ and the compound statements $Q\\lor R$ and $P\\land (Q\\lor R).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054389 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9209c4e5-30e0-5933-9c41-32750b5301ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054389 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(\\land)$ and \"or\" $(\\lor)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A \\land B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is false, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $Q \\lor R$ is true, but the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∨R) & ≡\\text{false}∧\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∨\\text{false})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186389663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186389768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186496281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054641 #edb/r