186055585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054914 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054914 #edb/ref 1045 "The \"And\" and \"Or\" Connectives" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054914 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054914 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054914 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054914 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4dd99c93-ce32-53a9-b191-e8bddb7f8f7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186051859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186051862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186051865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1069 "q-178152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{{\\overset{P}{\\overset{⏞}{{3}^{2}=9}}\\,\\overset{∧}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{and}}}\\,\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{2\\text{ is rational}}}}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∧\\,Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P∧Q$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $(P∧Q)∧R$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b084eee-0807-5bb1-bc2e-918712bbc035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055061 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is true. Therefore, $P∧Q$ is true, and the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∧Q)∧R & ≡\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∧\\text{true})}}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055579 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055579 #edb/ref 1061 153494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055579 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4a197e18-2f93-5927-89e7-71b02eeb66ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055579 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055580 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055580 #edb/ref 1061 153495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055580 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9a7b96e3-5988-5977-a20a-8a97b636978b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055580 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055581 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055581 #edb/ref 1061 153498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055581 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c089550c-a72d-5a29-a351-4052cea239c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055581 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055582 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055582 #edb/ref 1061 153501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055582 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "237b49c1-2062-5a12-862e-cc6120dfe275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055582 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055583 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055583 #edb/ref 1061 153502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055583 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1023b546-9b0c-52d3-9454-3a5adbb094ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055583 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055584 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055584 #edb/ref 1061 153503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055584 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96ad2c2e-7a64-57d5-9f83-02022e8509c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055584 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055585 #edb/ref 1061 153506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055585 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3cd4f3c8-8abb-53a5-a3a4-5df352b82883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055585 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056005 #edb/ref 1064 "A **compound statement** is a sentence that consists of two or more statements separated by logical connectors, such as the word \"and\" or the word \"or.\"\n\nFor example, the following sentence is a compound statement:\n\n$P: 2$ is an integer **and** $2$ is positive \n\nThe first statement is \"$2$ is an integer,\" and the second is \"$2$ is positive.\" These two statements are separated by the logical connector \"and.\"\n\nThe following sentence is also a compound statement:\n\n$7$ is odd **or** $7$ is even \n\nIn this case, the first statement is \"$7$ is odd,\" and the second statement is \"$7$ is even.\" These two statements are separated by the logical connector \"or.\" \n\nWe can express the logical connectives \"and\" and \"or\" using symbols:\n\n- The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land$\". Notice that it resembles \"A\" for \"And.\"\n\n- The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor$\".\n\nLet's translate the following sentence into symbolic form:\n\n$2$ is an integer **and** $2$ is positive \n\nTo start, we introduce the letters $A$ and $B$ to denote each individual statement:\n\n- $A:$ $2$ is an integer\n\n- $B:$  $2$ is positive\n\nThen, our sentence becomes\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is an integer} }_A \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{2 \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is positive} }_B,\n$$\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nFinally, note the following terminology:\n\n- The statement \"$P$ and $Q$\" is called the **conjunction** of the statements $P$ and $Q.$\n\n- The statement \"$P$ or $Q$\" is called the **disjunction** of the statements $P$ and $Q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056005 #edb/ref 1065 7962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056005 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "4570766f-a355-5a80-9756-cd94d76fed9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056005 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056029 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's now consider the truth values of the logical connector \"and\". We have the following key idea:\n\n*The statement $A \\land B$ is true if $A$ is true **and** $B$ is true. Otherwise, it is false.* \n\nLet's determine the truth values of the following compound statement:\n\n$2$ is positive **and** $2$ is even.\n\nWriting this in symbols, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nor, simply\n\n$$\nA\\land B.\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧B≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this context, the symbol \"$\\equiv$\" means \"is logically equivalent to.\" \n\nLet's now consider a similar compound statement but with the $2$ replaced with a $3$ in the second statement.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write this symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\nA\\land C\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $C$ is false, this compound statement is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧C≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056029 #edb/ref 1065 8142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056029 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e16d77df-210e-5934-90ce-44b096916261" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056029 #edb/ref 1067 "Truth Values of Statements Containing the \"And\" Connective" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056072 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's now consider the truth values of the logical connector \"or\". We have the following key idea:\n\n*The statement $A \\lor B$ is true if $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true. Otherwise, it is false.* \n\nLet's consider some examples:\n\n- First, consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true and $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨B≡\\text{true}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨C≡\\text{true}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Now, consider the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{-2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{D}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $B$ is true, this compound statement is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∨B≡\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, consider the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{-2\\text{ is positive}}_{⏟}}_{D}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D$ and $C$ are both false, this compound statement is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D∨C≡\\text{false}∨\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056072 #edb/ref 1065 9044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056072 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3b0d24cd-f605-59b2-9f16-f053e9b74e8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056072 #edb/ref 1067 "Truth Values of Statements Containing the \"Or\" Connective" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186379016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186379019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186379022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175912" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{{3\\,|\\,9}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\,|\\,16}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∧B$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc4b578b-6250-5651-a423-a5ab765ad427" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379015 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{3\\,|\\,9}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\,|\\,16}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379016 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379016 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379016 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186379018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379016 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d51318db-0570-5f7c-be3d-fcaf41b4d016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379017 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379017 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379017 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "df22f795-a009-5641-a379-443361928638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379018 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379018 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379018 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "de633a70-3263-5034-98fb-d53bce172bf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186379019 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186379020 #edb/ref 1759218